# Terminal — Opt+Return → bare Ghostty; Opt+Shift+Return → Ghostty in the shared
# `main` tmux session (docs/keybindings.md canonical terminal).
# WM-agnostic: common.skhd stays loaded across the Nehir/OmniWM run-one switch
# (and under other enabled macOS WMs). The canonical terminal chord is reserved
# for Ghostty here, not by either WM's native hotkey configuration.
# `open -na` opens a new window each press (macOS has no CLI to add a window to
# the running instance — Ghostty's +new-window is Linux-only); the per-launch
# --window-save-state=never stops that instance from restoring the previous
# window's tabs, so each press is a clean window.
alt - return : open -na Ghostty.app --args --window-save-state=never
shift + alt - return : open -na Ghostty.app --args --window-save-state=never -e tmux new -A -s main

# App tier — cross-platform letters (docs/keybindings.md): s/d/e/v/z/t/c
# match the Linux Ctrl+Super binds; c is the platform's Chromium-family
# browser (Arc here). m/w/x/r are macOS-local extras.
cmd + ctrl - s : open -a Slack
cmd + ctrl - d : open -a Discord
cmd + ctrl - e : open -a Element
cmd + ctrl - v : open -a Obsidian
cmd + ctrl - z : open -a Zen
cmd + ctrl - t : open -a Ghostty
cmd + ctrl - c : open -a Arc
cmd + ctrl - m : open -a Airmail
cmd + ctrl - w : open -a WhatsApp
cmd + ctrl - x : open /System/Applications/Music.app
cmd + ctrl - r : open /System/Applications/Reminders.app
